BUILD: midcentury: a mid-century modern single-family home (1950s-60s California, Eichler or Palm Springs style), single storey on a flat suburban lot, with a car parked in the driveway. Recognisable elements: a low, long horizontal form under a very low-pitched gable or flat/butterfly roof with deep overhanging eaves and exposed beam ends; a carport or garage with a sleek two-tone 1950s-60s car parked on a concrete driveway in front of it; walls of floor-to-ceiling glass with thin dark posts at the back facing the garden; a mostly blank street facade with a clerestory strip, a feature wall of stone or patterned breeze block, and a bold-coloured front door (orange, teal or yellow); post-and-beam structure; an open atrium or courtyard at the centre; a kidney-shaped pool and patio behind; desert or drought planting out front (cacti, gravel, a palm or two), a low mailbox and a path of stepping pads. Inside: an open-plan living room with a sunken conversation pit and a freestanding fireplace; dining area and a galley kitchen with a breakfast bar; three bedrooms along a corridor; two bathrooms; warm wood panelling, terrazzo or polished floors, period furniture (low sofas, an egg chair, a sideboard).
SIZE: about 34 wide (front, x), 34 deep including the front yard and back pool, 8 tall; 1:1 scale, a player is 2 blocks tall.
